      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T19:53:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks good, but when we start running the [EC unit tests](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/_/chromium/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/db551dae11cbcf1a8fa4e57b92480dc7d04f309b:board/hatch_fp/build.mk;l\u003d28-78) on Zephyr, we\u0027ll want to make sure that the RTC is enabled for the RTC unit tests [1](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/test/rtc_stm32f4.c;drc\u003d42ac2e87ae35b073d9a3aa571ac59acb028e8f54) and [2](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/test/rtc_npcx9.c;drc\u003ddef51a7ab9cd438c2590770205043c8b26bcb849).",
      "revId": "f97da467b1624e10ddfb7e561b0e9aa440a1e834",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02391122_60fede2e",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/fpmcu/bloonchipper/src/power.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T21:01:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You should take these values from [DTS](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/dts/arm/st/f4/stm32f4.dtsi#L515) using `STM32_DT_INST_CLOCKS()` macro (or `STM32_CLOCK_INFO()` if only APB1 clock should be disabled), instead of providing register and bit here.\n\nUnfortunately, the bit in DTS is different. According to the reference manual (RM0402 Rev 6 6.3.13) your version is correct.\n\nHave you considered disabling LSI clock?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "f97da467b1624e10ddfb7e561b0e9aa440a1e834",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
